            { text: "are equal to each of the straight lines {BX} and {XK|KX}.",
              highlighted: ["XP","XS","BX","KX"] },
            // Joyce's slip, left literal: "radius on of" for "radius one of".
            { text: "Therefore the circle with center {X} and radius on of the straight lines {XB|BX} or {XK|KX}",
              visible: CIRC,
              highlighted: ["Xcirc","X","BX","KX"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "Xcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] } },
            { text: "passes through {P} and {S} also,",
              highlighted: ["Xcirc","P","S"] },
            { text: "and {KBPS} is a quadrilateral in a circle.",
              highlighted: ["KBPS","Xcirc"] },
            { text: "Now, since {KB|BK} is greater than {WV|VW}, and {WV|VW} equals {SP}, therefore {KB|BK} is greater than {SP}.",
              highlighted: ["BK","VW","SP"] },
            { text: "But {KB|BK} equals each of the straight lines {KS} and {BP},",
              highlighted: ["BK","KS","BP"] },
            { text: "therefore each of the straight lines {KS} and {BP} is greater than {SP}.",
              highlighted: ["KS","BP","SP"] },
            { text: "And, since {KBPS} is a quadrilateral in a circle, and {KB|BK}, {BP}, and {KS} are equal, and {PS|SP} less,",
              highlighted: ["Xcirc","BK","BP","KS","SP"] },
            { text: "and {BX} is the radius of the circle,",
              highlighted: ["Xcirc","BX"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {KB|BK} is greater than double the square on {BX}.",
              highlighted: ["BK","BX"] },
            { text: "Draw {KZ} from {K} perpendicular to {BV}.",
              visible: KZs,
              highlighted: ["KZ","BV"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "KZ", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angKZB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.12" }] },
            { text: "Then, since {BD} is less than double {DZ},",
              highlighted: ["BD","DZ"] },
            { text: "and {BD} is to {DZ} as the rectangle {DB|BD} by {BZ} is to the rectangle {DZ} by {ZB|BZ},",
              highlighted: ["BD","DZ","BZ"] },
            { text: "therefore if a square is described on {BZ} and the parallelogram on {ZD|DZ} is completed,",
              highlighted: ["BZ","DZ"] },
            { text: "then the rectangle {DB|BD} by {BZ} is also less than double the rectangle {DZ} by {ZB|BZ}.",
              highlighted: ["BD","BZ","DZ"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.46" }] },
            { text: "And, if {KD} is joined,",
              visible: KDs,
              highlighted: ["KD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "KD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angBKD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle BKD right", ref: "III.31" }] },
            { text: "then the rectangle {DB|BD} by {BZ} equals the square on {BK},",
              highlighted: ["BD","BZ","BK"] },
            { text: "and the rectangle {DZ} by {ZB|BZ} equals the square on {KZ}.",
              highlighted: ["DZ","BZ","KZ"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.8.Cor" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the square on {KB|BK} is less than double the square on {KZ}.",
              highlighted: ["BK","KZ"] },
            { text: "But the square on {KB|BK} is greater than double the square on {BX},",
              highlighted: ["BK","BX"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {KZ} is greater than the square on {BX}.",
              highlighted: ["KZ","BX"] },
            { text: "And, since {BA|AB} equals {KA}, therefore the square on {BA|AB} equals the square on {AK|KA}.",
              highlighted: ["AB","KA"] },
            { text: "And the sum of the squares on {BX} and {XA|AX} equals the square on {BA|AB},",
              visible: ZAs,
              highlighted: ["BX","AX","AB","angAXB"] },
            { text: "and the sum of the squares on {KZ} and {ZA} equals the square on {KA},",
              highlighted: ["KZ","ZA","KA","angKZB"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the squares on {BX} and {XA|AX} equals the sum of the squares on {KZ} and {ZA},",
              highlighted: ["BX","AX","KZ","ZA"] },
            { text: "and of these the square on {KZ} is greater than the square on {BX},",
              highlighted: ["KZ","BX"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder, the square on {ZA}, is less than the square on {XA|AX}.",
              highlighted: ["ZA","AX"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.47" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {AX} is greater than {AZ|ZA}. Therefore {AX} is much greater than {AG}.",
              highlighted: ["AX","ZA","AG"] },
            { text: "And {AX} is the perpendicular on one base of the polyhedron, and {AG} on the surface of the lesser sphere,",
              highlighted: ["AX","KBPS","AG","sphLesser"] },
            { text: "hence the polyhedron does not touch the lesser sphere on its surface.",
              highlighted: FACES.concat(["sphLesser"]) },
            { text: "Therefore, given two spheres about the same center,",
              highlighted: SPH.concat(["A"]) },
            { text: "a polyhedral solid has been inscribed in the greater sphere which does not touch the lesser sphere at its surface.",
              highlighted: FACES.concat(["sphGreater","sphLesser"]),
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
